Supported Operators

Unlike nodeSelector, which only allows exact key-value matches, Node Affinity supports several logical operators in matchExpressions:
• In: The label's value must match at least one value in your specified list.
• NotIn: The label's value must not match any value in your list. (Useful for node anti-affinity).
• Exists: The node must have a label with the specified key, regardless of its value.
• DoesNotExist: The node must not have a label with the specified key.
• Gt (Greater Than): The label's value (parsed as an integer) must be greater than your specified value.
• Lt (Less Than): The label's value (parsed as an integer) must be less than your specified value.

