Node Affinity vs. Other Scheduling Features

• nodeSelector: The simplest approach for exact key-value matching. If you specify both nodeSelector and nodeAffinity on the same Pod, both must be satisfied.
• Taints and Tolerations: Node Affinity attracts Pods to specific nodes. Taints and Tolerations work in reverse—nodes repel Pods unless the Pod explicitly tolerates the taint. They are often used together to create dedicated node pools (e.g., tainting GPU nodes so normal workloads stay off, while using Node Affinity to pull GPU workloads onto them).

